//CTP Editor Structure file
//This file is the most commented one
//Same comments apply to other .ces files

//Booleans can be in 0/1 form or t/f form
//Any string whose first character is a '0' or 'f' is false,
//any other string is true

0.3 //Version number

#%047%047	//Comment charachter in data file
%032%009	//Delimiter charachters in data file
		// (use %nnn for ASCII ref)
:		//Break on right quasi-delimiter
}{		//Break on left quasi-delimiter

1 //Format - 0 for none (e.g. Const.txt)
  //         1 for usual entries and fields (like advance.txt)
  //         2 for Strings.txt
  //         3 for entries with just one associated value
  //           (e.g. sounds.txt)

f //Whether this has a number at the top (num of entries)
t //Whether this has a tree structure (see below)
t //Whether this file references GL entries (see below)
t //Whether this file has entries in gl_str.txt
//You only need include the following line if the previous is true
f //Whether the entries have an article
f //Whether this file is the GL icon file
t //Whether this structure file describes formatting of fields
  // (i.e. whether it has the next item and LBF and LAF columns below)

1 //New lines at the start of an entry (between the '{' and the first field instance)
2 //New lines between each entry

//For each field we have:
//Comp=Whether field is compulsory in every entry
//PByDef=Whether field present by default (in newly generated entry)
//AMult=Whether field may appear repeatedly in same entry
//LBF=New lines betwen field instances of this type
//LAF=New lines after the last field instance of this type
//NumArgs=Number of arguments to field.  Arguments listed below each.
//Name			Comp	PByDef	AMult	LBF	LAF	NumArgs
Prerequisites		f	f	t	1	1	1
	//For each argument we have:
	//Type=0 for 'ordinary' entry
	//     *<file name> for sub-structure with file reference
	//     <file name> for reference to entry of another file
	//Type		DefaultValue	Comment
	advance.ces	ADVANCE_	Prerequisite advance(s) for this
Cost			t	t	f	1	1	1
	0		20		Advance cost in commerce points
Icon			t	t	f	1	1	1
	uniticon.ces	ICON_%n		Icon id
Branch			f	f	f	1	1	1
	0		0		Does nothing
Age			t	t	f	1	1	1
	age.ces		AGE_ONE		Advance cost in commerce points
KeyAdvanceAdvice	f	f	f	1	1	1
	0		KEY_		String id of string displayed in science manager
PollutionSizeModifier	f	f	f	1	1	1
	0		1		Pollution modifier to be applied to Population pollution after this advance is discovered. 
PollutionProductionModifier	f	f	f	1	1	1
	0		1		Pollution modifier to be applied to Production pollution after this advance is discovered. 
TriggerFeat		f	f	f	1	1	1
	feat.ces	FEAT_		Feat ID of a Feat that is accomplished when this Advance is discovered. Must be a valid Feat ID from Feats.txt 
Capitalization		f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
Infrastructure		f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
Transform		f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
PlantNuke		f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
Roads			f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
Railroads		f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
MagLev			f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
Tunnels			f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
GLHidden		f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
DeepOcean		f	f	f	1	1	0	Comment
@ //End of fields

Prerequisites	//The defining field of the tree structure
		//and argument thereof
		// (include this only if tree structure true above)

//Now list other stuff to be listed in 'consequences':
//Tags must be distinct
//Tag	File		Field
(A)	advance.ces	Prerequisites
(I)	buildings.ces	EnableAdvance
(U)	units.ces	EnableAdvance
(W)	wonder.ces	EnableAdvance
(G)	govern.ces	EnableAdvance
(P)	pop.ces		EnableAdvance
(T)	terrain.ces	AddAdvance
//It would be nice if this worked:
//(TI)	tileimp.ces	TerrainEffect.EnableAdvance
//But it doesn't (yet...)
@ //End of cross references

Icon  //The field which references the GL icon entry in uniticon.txt
DATABASE_ADVANCES //Name of database for GL hyperlinks
ADVANCE_  //The prefix which identifies this file in gl_str.txt
